  "notes": "The two toolbar cases are par-macshell J0.20 toolbar-reply-all-opens-the-reply-box-with-everyone (checks/parity/par-macshell.py:493-495: clicks mac-main.toolbar.reply-all, reads the quick reply header open == 1 and a To filled) and toolbar-forward-opens-the-forward-window (:499: the forward composer opens, kind forward, subject starts 'Fwd: '); declared mutants :564-565 (WHOOSH_MUTANT_R8=dead-toolbar); the toolbar dispatch table Sources/Features/Shortcuts/Commands.swift:193-203 and ReplyDoors :224-246 (the same door as the key; fix-replydoors: Reply all reads the Reply-To through ReplyToRule.all, tests Tests/Unit/ReplyToDoorsTests.swift). par-macshell prints a line per case (print_cases). The earlier finding 'no toolbar lines in par-macshell-main83.log' is because r83 predates the line-per-case change (harness commit 8d4a5b1f): the cases exist and r83 had 0 failed. 'As the keys do': the key and the toolbar both call ReplyDoors (Commands.swift:224). The two mutants make the command do nothing: the case reads the visible outcome (box open with everyone / forward window with Fwd:) and goes red. real-compose (2026-11-12): the REAL engine now serves ReplyAll and SetSignature (core/crates/engine/src/compose_cmds.rs): proofs 1 and 2 are the engine's and the outbox's tests (core/crates/engine/tests/engine_compose_cmds.rs, core/crates/outbox/tests/reply_all.rs); the broken copies from the compose_cmds.rs, delta15.rs, rust_core.rs, outbox_tick.rs and reply adapter lines follow the fixture ones. Not run by the builder (no cargo). real-replyto (2026-11-12): the real engine keeps and uses a mail's Reply-To (migration 0027, store/src/reply_to.rs): proofs 3 to 5 are engine_reply_to (11 tests), sync-imap reply_to_stored (3) and store reply_to_0027 (8), with their broken copies after the real-compose ones; the migration's own tests (core/crates/store/migrations/tests/migration_v27_reply_to.rs, 2 tests) run in that crate's own workspace and have no proof line here. The three recipient broken copies of real-compose (To, Cc, sender lost) now name the new call `recipients_for_reply_all(...)`. Not run by the builder (no cargo)."
}